             border border-dashed border-white/60 rounded-full"
    >
      CERTIFIED ARBORIST SERVICES
    </span>

    <!-- TITLE -->
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl xl:text-6xl font-extrabold leading-tight">
      Certified Arborist Services
      <br class="hidden sm:block" />
      in South Florida
    </h1>

    <!-- SUBTEXT -->
    <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto text-lg text-white/90">
      Professional tree health assessments, arborist reports, permit guidance,
      and expert recommendations provided by certified arborists serving
      residential and commercial properties across South Florida.
    </p>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <div class="mt-14 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-6">

      <!-- PRIMARY -->
      <a
        href="/contact-us/"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-4 rounded-full
               bg-white px-12 py-5 text-teal-900 font-extrabold
               hover:bg-slate-100 transition"
      >
        Request Arborist Consultation
        <span
          class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full
                 bg-teal-900 text-white"
        >
          ↗
        </span>
      </a>

      <!-- SECONDARY -->
      <a
        href={`tel:${phone}`}
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-4 rounded-full
               border border-white/70 px-12 py-5 text-white font-bold
               hover:bg-white/10 transition"
      >
        📞 {phone}
      </a>

    </div>

    <!-- TRUST LINE -->
    <p class="mt-10 text-sm text-white/70">
      Licensed & insured · ISA-style professional standards · South Florida coverage
    </p>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= WHAT A CERTIFIED ARBORIST DOES ================= -->
<section class="bg-[#f4f8f6] py-32">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6">

    <!-- HEADER -->
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center mb-20">
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-8">
        What Does a Certified Arborist Do?
      </h2>

      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        A certified arborist is a trained tree care professional specializing in
        tree health, safety, and long-term management. Unlike standard tree
        services, arborists evaluate biological, structural, and environmental
        factors to make informed, professional recommendations.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- CONTENT GRID -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-10">

      <!-- CARD -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-10 shadow-sm">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-4 text-center">
          Tree Health Assessment
        </h3>

        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-center">
          Arborists evaluate tree health by inspecting roots, trunk structure,
          canopy condition, and signs of disease, decay, or pest infestation.
          This allows early detection of problems that may compromise safety or
          long-term tree stability.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- CARD -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-10 shadow-sm">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-4 text-center">
          Risk & Safety Evaluation
        </h3>

        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-center">
          Certified arborists identify structural weaknesses such as cracks,
          cavities, leaning trees, or compromised root systems. These risk
          assessments help determine whether pruning, bracing, or removal is
          necessary to protect people and property.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- CARD -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-10 shadow-sm">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-4 text-center">
          Professional Recommendations
        </h3>

        <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed text-center">
          Based on industry standards and local regulations, arborists provide
          expert recommendations for tree preservation, pruning, treatment, or
          removal. Every decision is guided by safety, compliance, and long-term
          tree health.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- EXPANDED TEXT -->
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto mt-20 space-y-8 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">

      <p>
        In South Florida, certified arborist services are especially important
        due to hurricanes, tropical storms, saturated soils, and fast-growing
        tree species. Arborists understand how local conditions affect root
        stability, wind resistance, and overall tree performance.
      </p>

      <p>
        Certified arborists are often required when applying for tree removal
        permits, preparing arborist reports for municipalities, or evaluating
        protected and heritage trees. Their assessments provide the technical
        documentation needed to meet city and county regulations.
      </p>

      <p>
        By working with a certified arborist, property owners receive unbiased,
        professional guidance focused on safety, compliance, and responsible
        tree management — not just tree removal.
      </p>

    </div>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <div class="mt-20 text-center">
      <a
        href="/contact-us/"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-4 rounded-full
               bg-teal-700 px-12 py-5 text-white font-extrabold
               hover:bg-teal-800 transition"
      >
        Schedule a Certified Arborist Consultation
        <span class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-white/15">
          ↗
        </span>
      </a>

      <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-slate-500">
        Serving residential & commercial properties across South Florida
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

